      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T15:38:34Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(geometry): expand DXF blocks (INSERT) on import\n\nAn INSERT of a BLOCK now places the block's geometry in world\ncoordinates: move, turn, X/Y/Z scale, column/row arrays and nested\nblocks. Arcs stay exact under a similarity; a mirror reverses them.\nUnequal scales lay circles and arcs as tangent arcs within the curve\ntolerance. Layer 0 takes the INSERT's layer. Cycles, missing blocks,\nnesting past 8 levels, copy counts past the vertex limit, zero or\nnon-finite values, a tilted extrusion and XREF blocks are refused by\nname.\n\nFixes #1865\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
