  {
    "sha": "9b384b67f8b630f2b313a7d55d445cb05202fbfe",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDliMzg0YjY3ZjhiNjMwZjJiMzEzYTdkNTVkNDQ1Y2IwNTIwMmZiZmU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T21:48:15Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T21:48:15Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(geometry): fit block curves after their INSERT placement\n\nA SPLINE or ELLIPSE in a block was fitted in block units before the\nplacement, and the placement scaled the fit error without a change of\nthe stated bound. The block body now keeps the curve definition. Each\nplaced copy maps it exactly (ellipse centre and axes, spline control\npoints) and fits it in world units within CURVE_TOLERANCE_MM.\n\nThe similarity shortcut to an exact circle now needs an exact matrix.\nA near similarity takes the ellipse path, which bounds the deviation\nin drawing units, or refuses the curve by name.\n\nPinned by tests/dxf/block_curves.rs (review of PR #4052).\n\nRefs #1865\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "9dc95a8940707d2f4b773a9ccde3aa5bca8da96e",
